msgid "Adds a Gallery section to the foot of every listing by that vendor, after the tags and before the reviews. Useful where the work itself is what sells the listing. Vendors with no gallery get no section at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:78
msgid "Gallery Button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:79
msgid "Show the photo count on the View Gallery button"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:80
msgid "With this off, the sidebar button simply reads \"View Gallery\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:87
msgid "Maximum Folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:88
msgid "Set the maximum number of gallery folders per vendor. Leave empty for no limit. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:95
msgid "Maximum Images per Folder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:96
msgid "Set the maximum number of images allowed in each folder. Leave empty for the default of 30. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:103
msgid "Videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:104
msgid "Allow uploading videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:110
msgid "Likes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:111
msgid "Let visitors like individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:112
msgid "Adds a heart button to every photo, with a count everyone can see. Only signed-in visitors can like, and each person can like a photo once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:119
msgid "AI Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:120
msgid "Review the first ten photos in each folder with AI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:121
msgid "Checks a folder's photos with OpenAI when the vendor saves the folder, using the API key from the HivePress Integrations settings. The first ten photos in the folder are checked together in one free request; any beyond the tenth are not checked. OpenAI fetches each photo from your site, so this only covers public folders: photos in private and members-only folders are skipped while Protect Files is on, because their files are not served at a public address. Your site must also be publicly reachable, so on local or private sites, and whenever the service is unavailable, saving simply proceeds unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:127
msgid "Comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:128
msgid "Let visitors comment on individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:129
msgid "Every photo gets its own page with a comment thread beneath it, where signed-in visitors can comment, reply and like comments. People can delete their own comments, and the folder owner can delete any comment on their photos."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:136
msgid "Protect Files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:137
msgid "Protect private and members-only image files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:138
msgid "Moves the files in private and members-only folders out of the folder your web server publishes, and serves them through an access-checked link instead, so there is no direct address to open. New uploads also get unguessable file names, and gallery images are excluded from public media API results. Recommended. If the files cannot be moved out on your hosting, a notice above says so and explains what to do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:145
msgid "Button Corner Rounding (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:146
msgid "Rounds the corners of every button this plugin adds, so they match the rest of your site. Leave it empty and each button keeps whatever shape your theme gives it, which is right on most sites. Set 0 for square corners, or a larger number for rounder ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:154
msgid "Maximum File Size (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:155
msgid "Reject gallery uploads larger than this many megabytes. Leave empty for no gallery-specific limit (the server upload limit still applies)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:162
msgid "Storage Limit (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:163
msgid "Cap the total disk space each vendor's gallery may use, counting every photo and its thumbnails. Vendors see their usage on their Gallery page. Leave empty for no cap. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:170
msgid "Allowed Image Formats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:171
msgid "Choose which image formats vendors may upload. Leave empty to allow all supported formats."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:185
msgid "Maximum Image Dimensions (pixels)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:186
msgid "Resize uploaded images so their width and height do not exceed this many pixels. Photos straight from a phone or camera are far bigger than any screen needs, so this is the single biggest saving; around 2000 suits most galleries. Leave empty to keep the original dimensions. For compression, WebP conversion and bulk work on images you already have, use a dedicated image plugin alongside this one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:204
msgid "Gallery Pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:205
msgid "How galleries look to visitors. These apply to the gallery page, to each folder page, and to the gallery sections you can add to vendor profiles and listing pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:210
msgid "Gallery Layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:211
msgid "Choose how the public gallery page displays folders. Folder covers gives each folder a cover picture in a grid, and every folder gets a page of its own. Single page puts every folder's photos on the gallery page one after another."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:217
msgid "Folder covers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:218
msgid "Single page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:223
msgid "Folder Columns"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:224
msgid "How many folder covers sit side by side on a full-width screen. Leave empty to fit as many as the screen allows, which is what a gallery did before this setting existed. Narrow screens always show fewer, so a phone is never asked to draw six columns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:240
msgid "Maximum Rows"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:241
msgid "Caps the folder grid where a gallery is shown inside another page, which is the Gallery section on vendor profiles and listing pages, and adds a link to the full gallery for whatever does not fit. Leave empty to show every folder. Needs a column count above, because rows only mean a number of folders once the columns are fixed. This deliberately does not apply to the gallery page itself: that page is the only route to a folder, so hiding folders there would leave them unreachable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:249
msgid "Cover Shape"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:250
msgid "The shape of each folder's cover picture. Horizontal suits landscapes, interiors and rooms; vertical suits portraits, fashion and hair. The picture is cropped to fit either way, so it is worth choosing the one your vendors mostly shoot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:256
msgid "Horizontal"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:257
msgid "Vertical"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:258
msgid "Square"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:263
msgid "Lightbox"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:264
msgid "Let visitors enlarge the photo on its page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:265
msgid "With this on, clicking the photo on its own page enlarges it in a pop-up viewer. Photos in the gallery always open their own page, where the comments live."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:272
msgid "Gallery Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:273
msgid "Adds a sidebar to the gallery page, showing the vendor's profile card. You can add your own widgets to it in the \"Gallery Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:279
#: includes/configs/settings.php:293
msgid "No sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:280
#: includes/configs/settings.php:294
#: includes/configs/settings.php:319
msgid "Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:281
#: includes/configs/settings.php:295
#: includes/configs/settings.php:320
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:286
msgid "Folder Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:287
msgid "Adds a sidebar to each folder page, showing the vendor's profile card. You can add your own widgets to it in the \"Folder Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:312
msgid "Photo Page Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:313
msgid "Choose which side of the photo page the sidebar sits on. It shows the vendor's profile card and, for the photo's owner, the editing options, so it cannot be switched off. You can add your own widgets to it in the \"Photo Page (sidebar)\" area under Appearance, then Widgets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:327
msgid "Gallery Monetisation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:328
msgid "Members-only folders are how galleries make money: visitors must unlock them before seeing inside. <strong>To charge through memberships</strong>, add the gallery privileges to a paid HivePress Memberships plan, or add them to a free plan to simply require an account. <strong>To let vendors charge instead</strong>, enable paid access below: a locked folder then offers that vendor's one-off purchase, and only vendors who have not set a price fall back to your upgrade page link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:333
msgid "Members-Only Folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:334
msgid "Let vendors mark folders as members-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:335
msgid "Members-only folders appear locked until a visitor gains access through a membership plan or a purchase. With this off, vendors only choose between public and private, and any existing members-only folders behave as private. Turn it off if your site has no plans to monetise galleries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:342
msgid "Locked Folder Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:343
msgid "Choose how members-only folders appear to visitors without access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:349
msgid "Show blurred previews"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:350
msgid "Show locked placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:351
msgid "Hide completely"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:356
msgid "Paid Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:357
msgid "Let vendors sell access to their members-only folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:358
msgid "Vendors set their own lengths and prices, choosing from a day, a week, a month, three months or permanent access, and may offer up to three of them at once. Setting any is optional. Buying is a normal WooCommerce checkout. While a vendor sells access, their locked folders show the purchase button rather than the upgrade page link. Requires WooCommerce. With HivePress Marketplace active, these sales count towards vendor earnings and your usual commission applies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:376
msgid "What Access Buys"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:377
msgid "Whole gallery: a vendor sets one set of prices on their Gallery page and a buyer unlocks all of that vendor's members-only folders at once. Each folder separately: a vendor sets prices on each folder's own page and a buyer unlocks only the folder they paid for. Prices set under one choice are kept if you switch to the other and back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:384
msgid "The vendor's whole gallery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:385
msgid "Each folder separately"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:390
msgid "Commission Rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:391
msgid "Your percentage of a gallery access sale. Leave both commission boxes empty to take none. The amount is added on top at checkout and shown to the buyer as a separate line called Platform fee, so the vendor still receives the price they set. This only reaches you if your payment gateway settles gallery orders into the site's own payment account, which is the normal case. If you use a gateway that charges each vendor's connected account directly, the whole order including this fee is paid to the vendor and none of it reaches the site, so leave both boxes empty and take your cut through that gateway instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:400
msgid "Commission Fee"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:401
msgid "A flat amount on top of the rate, charged once per gallery access sale. Use either box on its own or both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:408
msgid "Upgrade Page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:409
msgid "Choose the page locked visitors are sent to, e.g. your membership pricing page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:419
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:420
msgid "Your galleries are kept if you ever delete this plugin. WordPress shows its own warning saying that deleting a plugin also deletes its data, but that warning is generic: it appears for every plugin and does not describe what this one does. Nothing below is removed unless you tick the box first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:425
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:426
msgid "Delete folders, likes, comments and settings when this plugin is deleted (photos stay in your media library)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:427
msgid "Leave this unticked, and deleting the plugin keeps every gallery folder, photo, like, comment, purchased access and setting, so reinstalling brings your galleries back exactly as they were. Tick it, and deleting the plugin permanently removes all of that. Photos themselves always stay in your media library either way. This cannot be undone, so only tick it if you are sure you are finished with the gallery."
msgstr ""

